{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus","id":1048978,"title":"Doctor Johnathan Snow and that Pesky Consensus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-14T15:52:56-08:00","id":1048978,"title":"Doctor Johnathan Snow and that Pesky Consensus","content":"For those who don't know, &quot;Animolecules&quot; (the name given to microbes by some historical scientists) were well known as biological entities before their role in causing infectious disease was discovered. The theory of microbiotic infection was considered laughable; how could tiny little creatures, no bigger than a few micrometers across, make a person sick?<br /> <br /> Dr. Snow had a radical theory; some comma shaped animolecules (the bacteria which we now know cause Cholera) were behind the outbreaks of cholera in London. The prevailing theory of disease and infection was Miasma. Bad Airs made people sick, and thus elevation and clean sweet-smelling air would protect you. However, cholera struck people who would be in miasma-free areas, and spared many in &quot;dirty&quot; areas which would have Miasmas. Academics at the time would waffle for a few 100 pages about why the Miasmas behaved in contrived ways to make such outliers possible.<br /> <br /> Now... here is the problem with all of this in the context of Mage. Every big scientific discovery starts off as going against the grain. Dr. Snow had proof of this action, and was getting results from making changes which ONLY work in this model, long before any shift in consensus. The majority of the world was against him on this, including a great number of Awakened individuals (we can only assume, since the most powerful academic institutions in the most important city in the world MIGHT have had one or two Mages).<br /> <br /> So, we have two models which fit into the Mage Lore. One is that every Paradigm is equally right/wrong and that they are all equally good/bad ways of modelling and changing the world. The other is that while every Paradigm works, scientific paradigms are closer to the Earthly Foundations, the underlying nature of reality, since they go into great detail in attempts to record, understand and model them while some Paradigms just ignore them.<br /> <br /> Considering the way that scientific discovery just works (that is, the visible evidence of cholera in water which was taken from homes of people with the disease, and it being absent in water which isn't from diseased homes, and him shutting off water linked to the microbe stopped deaths, and that he could prove that putting faeces in water led to a rise in these little animolecules but even if you filtered the water of waste they would still have the microbes and STILL cause disease, ALL before anyone else in the world had even had such thoughts (for the purposes of this, possibly some isolated and less famous medics had similar theories but we can call them negligible since they were, if they were present at all), and thus there couldn't be a Consensus or anything generating this phenomenon), the latter concept simply has to be the case in Mage.<br /> <br /> Scientific Discoveries cause shifts in the Consensus not through a &quot;hey everyone believe in this and then it will start working&quot;, but first through &quot;hey this works, I have proof, everyone believe in it&quot;. The only way this argument doesn't stand up, from what I can see is some fan-fiction about Snow being a Technocracy Plant, and the Technocracy knowingly faking the existence of Microbial disease since their current idea on how diseases worked... just didn't... match up? That would make the Technocracy knowing bullshitters, and as far as I can see the Technocracy REALLY believe in Science, since that's the POINT of Paradigms. If you think your Paradigm is bullshit that you need to fake to shift consensus, then you're not Awakened.<br /> <br /> And let's be frank, if Consensus worked via method 1, the theory of Miasma would manifest in the real world and the treatments given by olde-time doctors would have WORKED. Pouring the waste of the city into the river would have purged illness from the streets. The fact that accepted, consensual models of reality don't match up with outcomes shows that the Earthly Foundations defy consensus in MILLIONS of ways. Gay people existing in times/places where they weren't an accepted feature of reality in many cultures. Hyper-intelligent children emerging from populations of uneducated slaves, unexpected diseases arising in ways that the current Consensus cannot allow for...<br /> <br /> Anyways, those are just my thoughts. All I can say is that Consensus is mostly relevant in deciding if things are Vulgar or not, and that Consensus can (in extreme cases) make shifting reality much, much easier. And I begrudgingly must accept the &quot;phones work because consensus&quot; line as a part of the Lore, and it's one I'm happy to include since it's a cool idea, however it doesn't change the fact that the very scientific method itself doesn't fit with Model #1 of Consensus at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T16:08:18-08:00","id":1048987,"title":"","content":"I agree that the Consensus should only be considered to influence True Magic and creatures whose physical form is created by True Magic (Bygones, Constructs, Familiars, etc). Beyond that, the Earthly Foundations are Reality, including mystical phenomena like Changelings, Fera, Kindred, Kuei-jin, Possessed, Sorcerers, Wraiths, etc. The Technocrats just created Paradigms that emulated some of the Earthly Foundations (the parts that they could control for power and profit) and have been trying to annihilate any evidence of Earthly Foundations that conflict with the Paradigms of the Technocrats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T16:44:11-08:00","id":1049003,"title":"","content":"Not surprisingly, I'm agreeing too. However, this is the point where others will say, that history and everything we know about it is a lie in the world of Mage and that the game's world is not the real world, etc.<br /> <br /> I would say the same I did on the other thread: Occam's razor. WoD and Mage is based on the real world, so if you have to alter/contradict/dismiss a lot of things that happened IRL, that's a less likely explanation to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T16:57:37-08:00","id":1049015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus#post1048978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those who don't know, &quot;Animolecules&quot; (the name given to microbes by some historical scientists) were well known as biological entities before their role in causing infectious disease was discovered. The theory of microbiotic infection was considered laughable; how could tiny little creatures, no bigger than a few micrometers across, make a person sick?<br /> <br /> Dr. Snow had a radical theory; some comma shaped animolecules (the bacteria which we now know cause Cholera) were behind the outbreaks of cholera in London. The prevailing theory of disease and infection was Miasma. Bad Airs made people sick, and thus elevation and clean sweet-smelling air would protect you. However, cholera struck people who would be in miasma-free areas, and spared many in &quot;dirty&quot; areas which would have Miasmas. Academics at the time would waffle for a few 100 pages about why the Miasmas behaved in contrived ways to make such outliers possible<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> Anyways, those are just my thoughts. All I can say is that Consensus is mostly relevant in deciding if things are Vulgar or not, and that Consensus can (in extreme cases) make shifting reality much, much easier. And I begrudgingly must accept the &quot;phones work because consensus&quot; line as a part of the Lore, and it's one I'm happy to include since it's a cool idea, however it doesn't change the fact that the very scientific method itself doesn't fit with Model #1 of Consensus at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's how it worked in our world. I can probably list a half a dozen other moments in history that shouldn't work if reality is subjective.<br /> <br /> But that's our world.<br /> <br /> Mage suspends all that and says that reality relies on the collective belief of humanity. It was bold and went beyond just 'magic works' and tried to give a reason based in Postmodernist thought. And yeah, because that idea is crazy it is going to have problems, and maybe the scientific method is more flawed then it appears there, but that doesn't invalidate the game.<br /> <br /> And I should point out that there are two elements of Mage that do help make events make more sense.<br /> <br /> Firstly, there is a secret, world-spanning conspiracy actively trying to seed ideas into society so that they can advance their ideas. They seed the academic and popular world with ideas so that when the moment is right they can trigger one of Kuhn's paradigm shifts. Because that kind of shift is indeed how scientific thought often advances. And I should point out that while the microbial theory was on shaky ground at the time, they had their other ducks in a row. Statistical analysis, microscopes, civic engineering, and a water company that just happened to ignore the law about where it got its water from* were all ready for when the outbreak hit.<br /> <br /> Secondly, while consensual reality is easy to say it's often a chaotic system with some ideas hanging on long after they should have died out and others taking root before the situation seems right. It's a lot like internet memes that way. We know what they are and why they are, but we can't easily predict what will and will not become a meme. Mages have the rough idea, but no one short of the Oracles know the details.<br /> <br /> *That was the lucky break that proved him right after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 02-14-2017, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T19:24:29-08:00","id":1049096,"title":"","content":"Sadly, no, it is very much stated EVERYWHERE on the Mage Lore that this is NOT the case.<br /> <br /> Go read the Sorcerers crusade, for example. Mostly, until the level 3 of any Sphere, the members of the Order of Reason only do stuff within some &quot;reasonable&quot; &quot;scientific&quot; principles.<br /> <br /> But things start getting trickier around level 4.<br /> <br /> So... Things like a vilisilicoi (I believe that's the name). Basically, a dark ages &quot;cellphone&quot;, a Correspondence 2 device used in almost all OoR lodges to allow for long distance communication.<br /> <br /> Here is the thing: the average Joe on the Technocracy doesn't know shit. That's the guy that believes that what he does is &quot;science&quot;.<br /> <br /> But, Control, the Ivory Tower, those guys on Autochtonia and Mecha and Tycoides, those guys on the top of the piramid, those know the craps they sell to the ones bellow. They DO know that their Paradigm is crap.<br /> <br /> Do you wanna know what REAL science is in the WoD?<br /> <br /> It's not the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Real science is what the Sons of Ether do. THAT'S the real stuff.<br /> <br /> But... The science of the SoE is the most subjective crap EVER. It's even more insane than the Dreamspeakers animism.<br /> <br /> The Technocrats dont try to figure out the truth; they have their own truth.<br /> <br /> And once again, if there is such a thing as a Paradigm &quot;closer&quot; to the Earthly Foundations, it would be the animistic view of groups like Dreamspeakers. Lets not forget that the most basically lore of WoD is that material and spiritual were united at some point in the past. So, &quot;spirits will&quot; is probably a FAR better answer than &quot;gravity&quot;, for example.<br /> <br /> So yes, the Technocracy is a bullshit organization.<br /> <br /> Proof? Well, gunpowder used to be a &quot;magikal&quot; substance during the Sorcerors crusade, and firearms were vulgar magik... No &quot;Earthly Foundations&quot; principles applyed to firearms, but a vulgar Forces effect of TRUE MAGIK, until the SHIFT IN CONSENSUS turned firearms into mundane things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T00:29:28-08:00","id":1049175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049096#post1049096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, no, it is very much stated EVERYWHERE on the Mage Lore that this is NOT the case.<br /> <br /> Go read the Sorcerers crusade, for example. Mostly, until the level 3 of any Sphere, the members of the Order of Reason only do stuff within some &quot;reasonable&quot; &quot;scientific&quot; principles.<br /> <br /> But things start getting trickier around level 4.<br /> <br /> So... Things like a vilisilicoi (I believe that's the name). Basically, a dark ages &quot;cellphone&quot;, a Correspondence 2 device used in almost all OoR lodges to allow for long distance communication.<br /> <br /> Here is the thing: the average Joe on the Technocracy doesn't know shit. That's the guy that believes that what he does is &quot;science&quot;.<br /> <br /> But, Control, the Ivory Tower, those guys on Autochtonia and Mecha and Tycoides, those guys on the top of the piramid, those know the craps they sell to the ones bellow. They DO know that their Paradigm is crap.<br /> <br /> Do you wanna know what REAL science is in the WoD?<br /> <br /> It's not the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Real science is what the Sons of Ether do. THAT'S the real stuff.<br /> <br /> But... The science of the SoE is the most subjective crap EVER. It's even more insane than the Dreamspeakers animism.<br /> <br /> The Technocrats dont try to figure out the truth; they have their own truth.<br /> <br /> And once again, if there is such a thing as a Paradigm &quot;closer&quot; to the Earthly Foundations, it would be the animistic view of groups like Dreamspeakers. Lets not forget that the most basically lore of WoD is that material and spiritual were united at some point in the past. So, &quot;spirits will&quot; is probably a FAR better answer than &quot;gravity&quot;, for example.<br /> <br /> So yes, the Technocracy is a bullshit organization.<br /> <br /> Proof? Well, gunpowder used to be a &quot;magikal&quot; substance during the Sorcerors crusade, and firearms were vulgar magik... No &quot;Earthly Foundations&quot; principles applyed to firearms, but a vulgar Forces effect of TRUE MAGIK, until the SHIFT IN CONSENSUS turned firearms into mundane things.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, why didn't the medical practices of the Purificationists, who had Consensus, work? They were cleaning the streets of filth and the outbreaks just got worse. By your logic their methods would have solved everything.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, someone who thinks that their paradigm is crap can't have Genius above... 1? Like they can grow to realise that the other paradigms are shifting forces that must be competed against, that consensus can be shaped, but &quot;science is made up&quot; isn't a thought someone with Genius 6 can ever have. If such elements exist in the lore, they're bullshit writing which fails to stick to the key message of Mage, that belief matters to Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-15-2017, 03:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T00:31:24-08:00","id":1049176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049003#post1049003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not surprisingly, I'm agreeing too. However, this is the point where others will say, that history and everything we know about it is a lie in the world of Mage and that the game's world is not the real world, etc.<br /> <br /> I would say the same I did on the other thread: Occam's razor. WoD and Mage is based on the real world, so if you have to alter/contradict/dismiss a lot of things that happened IRL, that's a less likely explanation to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather make WoD our world with additions and some substitutions. Endron instead of Shell, sure, but Snow fathered pathology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T03:14:18-08:00","id":1049206,"title":"","content":"Ahh, my dear consensus. It is such an interesting beast.<br /> <br /> It's also not as clean-cut and simple as one might think.<br /> Its inherent nature can range from a liberal and open whitelist-style approach of 'These things are definitely true' all the way to a restrictive, highly controlling blacklist-style situation of 'Only this is true, everything else is verboten'.<br /> <br /> On what point of the scale the consensus is shaping reality is defined by three things:<br /> * How widespread and global a certain belief is.<br /> * How strictly defined and detailed the belief is.<br /> * How hostile the belief is to undefined or contrary reality. This is, in parts, linked to the second bullet point as we'll see later.<br /> <br /> <br /> Let's take, for example, the situation in the OP regarding microbes causing illness;<br /> There is a big difference between a person or group going<br /> A) 'I believe tiny little beings inside people are making them ill'<br /> B) 'I believe *these* tiny little beings inside people are making them ill'<br /> C) 'See those little things inside people? We can see them making people ill.'<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Situation A<br /> -----------<br /> This one is is purely driven by belief.<br /> As in, there was no previous witnessing to this by the believer themselves; It is either something they came up with ( Be it based on pure imagination, or conclusion of exercize of their logic ), or something somebody told them, be it written or heard. The believer is also not looking for any kind of validation or proof. They are either faith-driven, simply believe what they heard or read, or simply utterly confident in their own logic.<br /> <br /> This is the kind of situation where a critical mass of believers literally creates a new part of reality. It does not matter how things were before - in the area of influence of that critical mass of believers, people get ill because of tiny little microbes.<br /> The only way this is prevented, is if a larger mass of sleepers in the same area are aware of this idea and actively disbelieve it.<br /> The amount of people that is required locally in an area to share a common belief to shape reality is undefined, although there are hints in the latest book that at least 100 people are required.<br /> <br /> <br /> Situation B<br /> -----------<br /> Ths one is is an in-between.<br /> There is a witnessing, an observation - namely that there are in fact little tiny things inside people. They are already there and part of reality. However wether they are actually causing illness or not is, at that moment, undefined. Maybe they do, maybe they don't. The belief is a lucky guess/conclusion, pure imagination or a rumor, more so than an observation.<br /> But, if the critical mass of supporters of this belief once more forms, and is not contested by a larger group, then the little microbes will start causing illness - if they've not already done so.<br /> <br /> <br /> Situation C<br /> -----------<br /> This one is what we would call the most logical approach - something gets actually witnessed and thus people *know* it happens.<br /> 'Know'. In the world of Mage this situation is more loaded and complex than you'd think;<br /> <br /> The witnessed event might simply be a very local part of reality instead of something global - a thing that was not contested by local belief: A possibility that is not actually a global, universally true thing.<br /> However, if those that witness it and document it spread this 'knowledge' and through their arguments and observations find a larger and larger mass of people that share this belief, then the rest of the world's reality is being molded as the idea spreads. See A / B.<br /> <br /> Even if what was witnessed was actually part of most of reality before already, the observation and spreading of the idea among sleepers will start pushing against the small areas where the behavior of reality so far was something else, while also cementing the status quo in the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course. All of the above also works in a negative sense:<br /> 'I do NOT believe tiny little beings inside people are making them ill. It's not true!'<br /> 'I do NOT believe *these* tiny little beings inside people are making them ill. It's not true!'<br /> That's not a big difference to the positive examples. These negative ones change as much a specific, single part of reality as the positive examples do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The drastic hardcore variants of denial, however, are where the can of worms is at:<br /> <br /> 'I believe tiny little beings inside people are making them ill. All those other things are false!'<br /> 'I believe *these* tiny little beings inside people are making them ill. All those other things are false!'<br /> 'See those little things inside people? We can see them making people ill. That means all those other things people claim are causing illness cannot be true!'<br /> <br /> And unlike the described situations where a new part of reality is shaped, or an existing part is changed, the drastically negative approach has a much more lasting effect; It takes away from Reality. It lessen possibilities by saying that certain things are not possible, by denying the existance of the things that were not witnessed.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> <br /> The TL;DR of it all is:<br /> <br /> Reality is not a computer that *only* does the things that people believe in.<br /> Reality is like a little child that can and will do all sorts of things. Perhaps it will do things a specific way in front of its aunt, or might not do a specific thing in front of its strict stepdad. But kids will try all sorts of fancy things.<br /> <br /> Even a neutral set of opinion along the lines of 'Illnesses are caused by tiny beings in your body' and 'Spirits are causing illness' are not per see clashing - after all it could be the spirits placing them there.<br /> <br /> Until somebody restricts this reality child, gives it a defined, big list of rules what it can and (more importantly) cannot do, and tries to increase both lists every time they think something unacceptable happened, in order to make sure only things they want to happen do happen.<br /> And that's how the Technocracy tries to control and 'define' reality, removing possibilities according to the Sixth(?) Precept Of Damian, <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T03:39:06-08:00","id":1049210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049175#post1049175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, why didn't the medical practices of the Purificationists, who had Consensus, work? They were cleaning the streets of filth and the outbreaks just got worse. By your logic their methods would have solved everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said it didn't?<br /> <br /> Also, there was no single unified dominant Paradigm before.<br /> <br /> Another thing is, the techie's don't want to CURE all diseases. At least, not yet. Some day, yes. But not now. At the present, diseases are a great tool to keep the technocratic Consensus up to date. I tell you, it is not impossible to find archmages that will claim that mundane germ spread diseases is a creation of the Technocracy so that they could create <i>medicine</i> in order to control the masses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049175#post1049175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, someone who thinks that their paradigm is crap can't have Genius above... 1? Like they can grow to realise that the other paradigms are shifting forces that must be competed against, that consensus can be shaped, but &amp;quot;science is made up&amp;quot; isn't a thought someone with Genius 6 can ever have. If such elements exist in the lore, they're bullshit writing which fails to stick to the key message of Mage, that belief matters to Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are not. You could say that there are TWO different &quot;Technocratic paradigms&quot; within the Union. One is that of the agents, the ones at the base of the piramid. The one they sell to the masses. That's science. The other is the paradigm of the top. Of those guys who represent that big eye on the top of the piramid. That's the Paradigm of Control, of the Ivory Tower, the Paradigm of the guys who REALLY knows what's going on. And those have a Paradigm which is much more like the Etherite Science. They KNOW that science is &quot;personal&quot; - and that's exactly why they supress it, that's why they keep time tables on it, in order to CONTROL it. They know EXACTLY what they are doing, those guys are NOT deluded fools believing in a made up bullshit. On contrary, they make things up BECAUSE they know how it works. Meaning: Control could do EXACTLY the same insane things as the Etherites or VAs. But, they consider it too dangerous, which is why they keep their time table about what should or should not become &quot;reality&quot;. Those things that they deem too dangerous, will simply become &quot;reality banned&quot;. So... Spirits? Nah, that shit is not real. And if you see one, it's just a trick. Mind reading? Oh please, don't make me laugh. Except that, when you become an agent of NWO and get enough clearance, your supervisor will call you privately to share some top secret informativo about telepathy and the scientific studies about psychic emanations, that simply aren't avaiable for lesser ranked officers within the Union. Souls are superstitious talk... Unless you reach a very high rank within the Union that will give you access to that information. But the typical Men in Black in the frontlines doesn't need to know that he has a &quot;soul&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T04:48:17-08:00","id":1049228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049175#post1049175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, why didn't the medical practices of the Purificationists, who had Consensus, work? They were cleaning the streets of filth and the outbreaks just got worse. By your logic their methods would have solved everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the problem. The Consensus may have said that cleaner meant healthier, but it also said that epidemics happen. In fact, forget the purificationists, the biggest problem is that the Consensus thought epidemics were unstoppable. The medical community, such as it was, may have been trying but they knew they didn't have a handle on it. The rest of the population certainly didn't think they did.<br /> <br /> That might have been the Technocracy's way in, by the way. Epidemics were unstoppable but they did run their course. By waiting for a lull or for some strange pattern that would inevitably emerge, they could time their releases and claim credit. Actually, the purificationists were probably their doing too. They could have had several explanations waiting in the works so that one of them was likely to catch on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, someone who thinks that their paradigm is crap can't have Genius above... 1? Like they can grow to realise that the other paradigms are shifting forces that must be competed against, that consensus can be shaped, but &quot;science is made up&quot; isn't a thought someone with Genius 6 can ever have. If such elements exist in the lore, they're bullshit writing which fails to stick to the key message of Mage, that belief matters to Mages. </div> </div> </div>This one is a really tricky one that depends a lot on how you approach, and I remember interminable arguments about if the Technocracy knew they were doing magic, with answers ranging from 'they are all fooling themselves' to 'they are just using the appearance of science' to 'most of them don't, but some of the more advanced ones so.' That last one tends to be where the arguments end up one way or another, since it gives the ST more options.<br /> <br /> You are also touching on one of the other questions of Mage here, which is how many conflicting things can be true at the same time. That's a fun one because most people have answered it in their heads even though they never realized it had been asked. As far as I am aware, the four possible answers are: one, more than one, none, and all. Which one do you think it is?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T06:11:36-08:00","id":1049261,"title":"","content":"I think that, in general, it is a mistake to think of the local paradigm being &quot;with&quot; any particular statement of <i>fact </i>rather than any particular methodological <i>approach</i>. It's immaterial to the materialist paradigm whether disease is caused by Farr's miasma or Snow's contaminated water, and it is possible <i>within a paradigm </i>for statements of belief, even widely-held ones, to be incorrect. This is why Revised draws a distinction between the two (belief vs. paradigm.)<br /> <br /> In a Classic Grecian paradigm it would be equally plausible for the community to believe that they were being blighted with disease because they had offended God A when, in fact, they had offended God B. Paradigm brackets how one investigates and articulates these causes, not what the specific cause in a given situation <i>is. </i>The lone-wolf religious specialist that agitated for propitiation of God B would similarly be going against the public grain, only to be proven right in time. This does not prove that the Classic Grecian paradigm is the underlying fundamental reality of the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T07:06:11-08:00","id":1049280,"title":"","content":"With regards to the Consensus and Mage, I think of Consensus as more of determining How the world usually works than forcing every aspect of reality to conform to its expectations. No matter how established and all-encompassing it seems to be, there will always be those flukes and strange events end phenomena that defy it.<br /> <br /> But with regards to Dr. Snow, isn't this how it would have gone in the story of Mage: The good doctor observes strange microscopic creatures using his scientific tools, comes up with the idea that they cause disease, and fights an uphill battle to prove that a certain bunch of these do in fact cause cholera. Wherever he &quot;personally&quot; makes an experiment to prove the case, either he finds that the results fit his hypothesis or else something has contaminated his test results. Of course, the technocracy only publishes his side of the story and begins the long program of getting rid of any evidence that Dr. Snow's results are anything but the truth. Other technocrats make the same experiments with the same results. Eventually people in a small area come to like and believe the idea that the cause of cholera is some living tiny creature that they could eventually find a way to kill. The idea gains traction and the concept of miasma starts to flounder, helped along by technocracy's publishing of cases wherein the miasma theory was disproved (either completely made up stories or cases where healing magic or other treatments screwed up.) Eventually. the lie becomes the truth and it is as if miasma was never a valid vector for disease to begin with. Disease that still manages to get transferred by &quot;bad air&quot; air can be explained off as being transferred by airborne animalcules and flying insects and such and the idea sticks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T08:02:10-08:00","id":1049300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049280#post1049280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With regards to the Consensus and Mage, I think of Consensus as more of determining How the world usually works than forcing every aspect of reality to conform to its expectations. No matter how established and all-encompassing it seems to be, there will always be those flukes and strange events end phenomena that defy it.<br /> <br /> But with regards to Dr. Snow, isn't this how it would have gone in the story of Mage: The good doctor observes strange microscopic creatures using his scientific tools, comes up with the idea that they cause disease, and fights an uphill battle to prove that a certain bunch of these do in fact cause cholera. Wherever he &quot;personally&quot; makes an experiment to prove the case, either he finds that the results fit his hypothesis or else something has contaminated his test results. Of course, the technocracy only publishes his side of the story and begins the long program of getting rid of any evidence that Dr. Snow's results are anything but the truth. Other technocrats make the same experiments with the same results. Eventually people in a small area come to like and believe the idea that the cause of cholera is some living tiny creature that they could eventually find a way to kill. The idea gains traction and the concept of miasma starts to flounder, helped along by technocracy's publishing of cases wherein the miasma theory was disproved (either completely made up stories or cases where healing magic or other treatments screwed up.) Eventually. the lie becomes the truth and it is as if miasma was never a valid vector for disease to begin with. Disease that still manages to get transferred by &quot;bad air&quot; air can be explained off as being transferred by airborne animalcules and flying insects and such and the idea sticks.</div> </div> </div> </div>However the Technocracy is trading &quot;disease is spread by bad air&quot;, something they can find a consensual fix for (incenses, masks, chemicals) for &quot;disease is spread by bad air, bad water, bad human contact, bad food, farm animals...&quot;. I can't see their motivation for the &quot;trade&quot;. Surely better to stick to an existing consensus?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, if you used Time to go back to the 1200s, and examined something with a microscope (let's call this the Time Travelling Histologist Problem), would you see microbes? Were microbes only a thing after a certain point? Did Snow imagine vibrio cholerae into existence?<br /> <br /> I think it's just much more simple to say that objective underlying reality is something that you can determine, and the Consensus can nudge it in certain directions but not overwrite it. Gravity exists, Stars burn hot, Paradox is a thing etc. Earthly Foundations are left vague so that an ST can make of this what they like. They can have a Histologist lost in a world without microbes, or our time traveler can die content in the fact that their paradigm has always been a thing.<br /> <br /> Another way out is to just say that reality is an illusion, but that's giving one Paradigm special superiority over the others... then again, my views of the Earthly Foundations are very pro-technomagick, and an objective answer on how reality actually is (or isn't) will always lean towards one paradigm or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T08:23:44-08:00","id":1049304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049261#post1049261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that, in general, it is a mistake to think of the local paradigm being &quot;with&quot; any particular statement of <i>fact </i>rather than any particular methodological <i>approach</i>. It's immaterial to the materialist paradigm whether disease is caused by Farr's miasma or Snow's contaminated water, and it is possible <i>within a paradigm </i>for statements of belief, even widely-held ones, to be incorrect. This is why Revised draws a distinction between the two (belief vs. paradigm.)<br /> <br /> In a Classic Grecian paradigm it would be equally plausible for the community to believe that they were being blighted with disease because they had offended God A when, in fact, they had offended God B. Paradigm brackets how one investigates and articulates these causes, not what the specific cause in a given situation <i>is. </i>The lone-wolf religious specialist that agitated for propitiation of God B would similarly be going against the public grain, only to be proven right in time. This does not prove that the Classic Grecian paradigm is the underlying fundamental reality of the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that, however the Lore repeatedly has things like &quot;technology stops working in certain Reality Zones&quot;, and has repeatedly said that phones only work because of the Technocratic paradigm being a prevailing one.<br /> <br /> It's useful to see a Paradigm as &quot;the way you see things&quot; (that's LITERALLY what it means), and a Mage universe where that's all Paradigm was would be cool... but I don't think that's the Mage world RAW. I might play it as that some day however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T08:52:08-08:00","id":1049313,"title":"","content":"(Look, I'll save you a lot of heartache and me a lot of heartache: There are places where pre-Revised Mage textually posits that the Technocratic model is genuinely predicated on the most basic foundational rules of Reality, full stop. This is in the first Book of Madness. You have officially received Papal Sanction to view the game in your preferred way. I do not think Revised follows this path, and I do not think it is either a necessary or a credible path for the game's thematic or practical interests.)<br /> <br /> I don't think Reality Zones are relevant to what I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> Are spirits real in the World of Darkness? (Don't get hung up on crossover rules or other game lines.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T08:55:54-08:00","id":1049316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049313#post1049313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Look, I'll save you a lot of heartache and me a lot of heartache: There are places where pre-Revised Mage textually posits that the Technocratic model is genuinely predicated on the most basic foundational rules of Reality, full stop. This is in the first Book of Madness. You have officially received Papal Sanction to view the game in your preferred way. I do not think Revised follows this path, and I do not think it is either a necessary or a credible path for the game's thematic or practical interests.)<br /> <br /> I don't think Reality Zones are relevant to what I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> Are spirits real in the World of Darkness? (Don't get hung up on crossover rules or other game lines.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, that might be a simpler approach. I've been... bothered by phones breaking down in the Amazon. Like the idea that Magick is what fuels every piece of tech ever is... well it almost feels like it's unfair to scientists and inventors?<br /> <br /> Well it kind of is, but only if you follow the M20 and Revised line on Reality Zones and how they affect tech, it's a null point if you don't.<br /> <br /> And Spirits are real in the sense that they are an observable phenomena, just one science hasn't really explained yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T09:26:59-08:00","id":1049324,"title":"","content":"It's important to understand that Technocracy isn't the scientific community. It's far, far, above the scientific community.<br /> <br /> Saying that, because the scientific comunity was against him, there were Awakened individuals against him it's a moot point. The Technocracy has been contradicting the beliefs of everyone since it's inception (remember when everyone believed in the heliocentric system). They manage to do so successfully in spite of Reality being (more or less) Consensual because they're a potent Awakened force that can change Reality. <br /> <br /> So, yes, starting an &quot;unstoppable&quot; plage that couldn't be cured by Consensual means, in order to prepare the stage for Doctor Johnathan Snow to heal it it's the kind of things they would do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've been... bothered by phones breaking down in the Amazon. Like the idea that Magick is what fuels every piece of tech ever is... well it almost feels like it's unfair to scientists and inventors? </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes it is. Having a monolithic conspiracy determining what's real and what's not it's quite unfair for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T09:44:11-08:00","id":1049333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049324#post1049324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's important to understand that Technocracy isn't the scientific community. It's far, far, above the scientific community.<br /> Yes, yes it is. Having a monolithic conspiracy determining what's real and what's not it's quite unfair for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, I mean in quite a meta sense. I feel like phones only working Because Consensus is a tad... so Sorcery and Magick rely on personal views of the world, and it doesn't devalue them to talk about the nature of belief. A regular Joe with no supernatural powers who invents something or deepens our scientific understanding (Lovelace for example, however as the first computer programmer and the daughter of Lord Byron I doubt you could call her an &quot;average Joe&quot;) does so from a place of rational thought and hard work, and there's something... special about that. A Universe which undermines the achievement of basically every great person of science is a bit... less fun almost?<br /> <br /> Like Religion, Science, Mysticism... they're all beautiful for different reasons. It would be nice to have an approach to Mage which made them very different as Paradigms, not the same Paradigm with a different aesthetic and varying Reality Zone Bonuses. Like Religious paradigms don't rely on beliefs being true. Two members of the Celestial Choir could think they were chosen by God to fight for justice and peace and love and truth... and they could end up on opposing sides of a bloody and meaningless conflict which God has nothing to do with. Their belief is very human, very flawed, and its flaws are its greatest assets. The person who thinks God chose them to kill every last Vampire/Demon/Werewolf is beautiful not because they're right, but because of the precise way they are wrong.<br /> <br /> Science, on the other hand is Correct. And... Correct in the most boring way possible. Read the introduction to Lore of the Clans if you want to get an idea of what I'm getting at; Facts vs Truths. Facts are dead, dry, boring things you can pin down. Truth is fluid and beautiful and dangerous and terrible. It might not be a fact that the Prince embraces and Diablerises humans on a weekly basis, but for the Neonates who tear down his haven and tear him to shreds it is certainly True in the moment. That, in my opinion, should be the underpinning difference between Scientific Paradigms and other Paradigms. You can explore why truth matters, and the value in things which aren't true but are useful (Parables for example aren't true, they make a point about the nature of the world however).<br /> <br /> &quot;We're right and we have proof&quot; is the cry of any Technocrat who happens to speak to a member of the Traditions... and the scary thing is that the Traditions don't care, nor should they. The scary thing is that the people who are technically right are BY FAR the most wrong. Such a system would focus a bit more on why being Rational and Correct aren't always good things, why humanity and warmth and wonder and spiritual belief matter even in the face of Cold Science. Imagine Dawkins as a Technocrat. Correct on Science, wrong on practically EVERYTHING else. The Orphan kid asking the Earth Mother to heal some injured protesters who are fighting to protect their native land is completely wrong about the true nature of reality, but that doesn't matter, nor should it. What matters is that she has power and she uses it for something that is Right to her. The Progenitor who sees such a scene and does nothing (why would they?) can go home and comfort themselves about how rational they are, but the overarching narrative I would hope to engender is that being the Winning Side in one sense can leave you the loser in every other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T10:04:16-08:00","id":1049342,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'm not gonna touch that with a ten-foot pole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049316#post1049316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well it kind of is, but only if you follow the M20 and Revised line on Reality Zones and how they affect tech, it's a null point if you don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Farr and Snow's dispute occurs within a single paradigm. Either could be right in a Technocratic Reality Zone, it just happens that one of them was.<br /> <br /> (I think being concerned with phones is liable to question-beg us back into your conclusion, so I'm mostly going to duck that for now, sorry.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049316#post1049316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Spirits are real in the sense that they are an observable phenomena, just one science hasn't really explained yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>So things exist in the Consensus which the masses do not acknowledge the existence of, and these things can be the cause of real effects.<br /> <br /> Following the argument of the original post, it then holds that Animism is the baseline rule of reality?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049316#post1049316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like the idea that Magick is what fuels every piece of tech ever is... well it almost feels like it's unfair to scientists and inventors?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is symptomatic of the greater issue: This is only a problem if your think magic is <i>fake</i>, and that discovery within a paradigm is a fraud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T10:30:30-08:00","id":1049358,"title":"","content":"I, personally, like to believe that you can invent/discover new stuff in Mage without being Awakened. That Technocracy (or Mages, for what matters) don't rule the world to such a deep extent.<br /> <br /> I, however, don't explain this as &quot;Science it's 100% true&quot;, but rather as normal people working within the constraints of a Paradigm, expanding said Paradigm and thus slowly shaping the world. What normal people do it's also magic, it's just that it's paved within the limitations of what's already believed to be possible or plausible. Anyone that reads sci-fi knows that this it's a big leeway.<br /> <br /> Sorcerers can do stuff that isn't quite accepted by the Consensus by exploiting fringe aspects of the Consensus. They can go further than any normal person with a lot of willpower and dedication (note that I don't put supernaturals in this same bag).<br /> <br /> Mages think outside the box, they don't need to respect the Consensus. Ironically, I see Mages as closer that normal people to the true rules of Reality, the Universal Constants set there by the Pures and other primeval beings.<br /> Opening their minds to the full potential of humans, Mages understand more clearly what's truly subjective and what isn't (No one can radically change Gravity without a lot of effort, so it must be real, at least to some extent. Germs?, those may be relative, perhaps they're bad spirits that got into your body). They don't know everything instantly, and are limited to their preconceptions, but they can probe further than anyone else, and whatever they can't change, it's probably there to stay.<br /> <br /> This way I recognize the labor of the Technocracy pushing their Paradigm and manipulating the advancement of science according to the Time Table, but also recognize that a mundane scientist may gave them a surprise once in a blue moon.<br /> <br /> Also, I mantain that all Paradigms are equally valid AND invalid. Reality exists, but only as underlying principles that sometimes agree with science, and sometimes resist it's methods but are more agreeable to different approaches to knowledge<br /> <br /> Of course, this it's just an idea. Plenty of stuff in the bibliography to go for a &quot;harder&quot; or &quot;softer&quot; reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-15-2017, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T12:27:19-08:00","id":1049424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049304#post1049304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You say that, however the Lore repeatedly has things like &amp;quot;technology stops working in certain Reality Zones&amp;quot;, and has repeatedly said that phones only work because of the Technocratic paradigm being a prevailing one.<br /> <br /> It's useful to see a Paradigm as &amp;quot;the way you see things&amp;quot; (that's LITERALLY what it means), and a Mage universe where that's all Paradigm was would be cool... but I don't think that's the Mage world RAW. I might play it as that some day however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage doesn't pinpoint it either way... And that's the beauty about it in my opinion. Unlikely Vampire, were you KNOW, as a player, that Saulot, Tzimisce, Tremere, Veddartha, Set, Haquim, or any other 3th generation are real - hell, you know even Cain is real, and in WtA you know Gaia and the Wyrm are real, in Mage they haven't gave out all the ultimate mysteries. So... Which is it? Is it The One? Well, it can be if you wanna it. Everything is a spirit? (gravity gafflings keep things on the soil, spirits of electromagnetism turn O2 into CO2 and so on). Is the world a matrix simulation, like say the VA? Is reality created by our perceptions, like claim the CoE and the SoE to a lesser extent? Or is reality bound by a rigid set of pr\u00ednciples, like claim the hermetics and technocrats?<br /> <br /> The answer can be one of those, parts of some of those or parts of all of those, or even none of those.<br /> <br /> That's the thing: each table is free to choose. That answer is not set on stone - on purpose. Which is what I find so great about Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T13:05:16-08:00","id":1049439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049300#post1049300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However the Technocracy is trading &amp;quot;disease is spread by bad air&amp;quot;, something they can find a consensual fix for (incenses, masks, chemicals) for &amp;quot;disease is spread by bad air, bad water, bad human contact, bad food, farm animals...&amp;quot;. I can't see their motivation for the &amp;quot;trade&amp;quot;. Surely better to stick to an existing consensus?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can get away from diseases just using incenses, you don't need the Technocracy. But, if diseases are such a complicated thing that you'll need a very specific science to study it, you just gave the Union a LOT of power over your own life. And the masses will gladly give themselves over the Union for it - not to mention that you can keep the entire humanity financially dependent of the Union's assets.<br /> <br /> Hell, to INVENT diseases would be the most genious move of the Union EVER.<br /> <br /> And even so, it may be a better alternative than having spirit-curse driven diseases... After all, it's easier to use antibiotics than performing exorcizes to heal people. It's a win-win situation for the Union (I know, now Aya will call them monsters for inventing the diseases. Well Aya, that's the price you have to pay for a safe world <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049300#post1049300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, if you used Time to go back to the 1200s, and examined something with a microscope (let's call this the Time Travelling Histologist Problem), would you see microbes? Were microbes only a thing after a certain point? Did Snow imagine vibrio cholerae into existence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats the thing: its up to YOU to answer that. The game leaves such an answer open for the players to say in any way they prefer.<br /> <br /> So... Yes, if you wanna it, in 1200 dc you'd see microbes, just the same as today, if you used a microscope. But, if you prefer, you wouldnt see... Because they didnt exist at that time. <br /> <br /> Mage is so incredible that their magic works in a quantum level IN THE REAL WORLD.<br /> <br /> We can say that Mage is the &quot;Schrodinger RPG&quot;; when you play, if you use Time 2 to analyse a tissue sample in the year 1.200, the presence of microbes are in a quantum state were it both exists/doesn't exist at the same time, until the player (and not the Mage) rolls the dice and the ST makes one of the instances collapse according to his expectations.<br /> <br /> Mage is so powerful, that the players/ST REAL LIFE persons (as oposed to the fictional chars) paradigms is what determines the reality.<br /> <br /> So, if your ST expect to see microbes on the 10th century, that's what you'll see. If he doesn't expect to see microbes in the dark ages, you won't.<br /> <br /> Mage is always on a quantum state of &quot;ST-biased&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049300#post1049300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think it's just much more simple to say that objective underlying reality is something that you can determine, and the Consensus can nudge it in certain directions but not overwrite it. Gravity exists, Stars burn hot, Paradox is a thing etc. Earthly Foundations are left vague so that an ST can make of this what they like. They can have a Histologist lost in a world without microbes, or our time traveler can die content in the fact that their paradigm has always been a thing.<br /> <br /> Another way out is to just say that reality is an illusion, but that's giving one Paradigm special superiority over the others... then again, my views of the Earthly Foundations are very pro-technomagick, and an objective answer on how reality actually is (or isn't) will always lean towards one paradigm or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's how it works for you, good for you. That's fine. You just collapsed the other quantum possibilities.<br /> <br /> Why can't reality be a Matrix?<br /> <br /> Well, can you see that your own personal answer is... Paradigm based? Lol. Nothing says it IS that... But... You... <i>Believe</i>. You, as a player. Not as a fictional character. You personally, are shaping the reality of Mage according to your personal Paradigm<br /> <br /> That shows that the game's premisses were highly successful in its efforts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T13:19:21-08:00","id":1049447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049313#post1049313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Look, I'll save you a lot of heartache and me a lot of heartache: There are places where pre-Revised Mage textually posits that the Technocratic model is genuinely predicated on the most basic foundational rules of Reality, full stop. This is in the first Book of Madness. You have officially received Papal Sanction to view the game in your preferred way. I do not think Revised follows this path, and I do not think it is either a necessary or a credible path for the game's thematic or practical interests.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I personally don't remember that. I'm not doubting you, I just don't know about that information<br /> <br /> I don't think Reality Zones are relevant to what I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049313#post1049313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are spirits real in the World of Darkness? (Don't get hung up on crossover rules or other game lines.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <br /> Actually, Mage has some very interesting consideration.<br /> <br /> Life, Matter, Forces<br /> <br /> Those 3 spheres are a hell lot better explained by Technocratic principles. Mystic ways just make those a lot harder to understand - that's true both to the mechanics (which lie outside of the fictional world and inside our real world) and to the set of the game (the lore of the fiction).<br /> <br /> I mean, it's far easier to say that you need Life 3+ for any group of vertebrates than trying to give some bullshit explanation about the subjective spiritual relevance of an octopus compared to a bear, compared to a shark, compared to a plant, and on and on and on...<br /> <br /> Spirit, Prime, Entropy<br /> <br /> Those spheres however, are a LOT better explained by mystical ways... To the point that the technocratic version of spirit is a bullshit pseudocience with the bullshit name of &quot;Dimensional Science&quot;.<br /> <br /> There you go: real life science - ie REAL science - doesn't have the study of some bullshit &quot;fifth essence&quot; that Plato said it were the higher thing that composed everything (a complement of the bullshit &quot;theory&quot; that everything is made of fire, air, water and dirty). And yet, the Technocracy have a &quot;scientific field&quot; devoted to study the bullshit totally fictional &quot;ether&quot; (and, by the way, the idea of said ether were banned by the Union itself, basically making everything about Prime to become vulgar).<br /> <br /> Real science also doesn't have vodoo like &quot;astral projections&quot;. And we are CERTANLY not made up of &quot;ether&quot; or &quot;quintessence&quot;. And, forgive me the believers, but what we are is what our brains make us. The moment the electricity stops in our brains, it's over. &quot;Soul&quot; is just a sweet self ilusion, a fairy tales for adults. However, in the game of Mage, it is &quot;science&quot; - dimensional science.<br /> <br /> So, a lot of Mage's &quot;sciences&quot; are, in fact, pseudoscientific bullshit with no more value as real knowledge than the Bible or Harry Potter or &quot;Astronaut Gods&quot; bullshit about annunnaki; Dimensional Science is as good a science as Astrology or Demonology.<br /> <br /> And yet, they are a VERY important part of the setting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-15-2017, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T13:31:02-08:00","id":1049450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049316#post1049316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haha, that might be a simpler approach. I've been... bothered by phones breaking down in the Amazon. Like the idea that Magick is what fuels every piece of tech ever is... well it almost feels like it's unfair to scientists and inventors?<br /> <br /> Well it kind of is, but only if you follow the M20 and Revised line on Reality Zones and how they affect tech, it's a null point if you don't.<br /> <br /> And Spirits are real in the sense that they are an observable phenomena, just one science hasn't really explained yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Phones don't exactly break down on the Amazon. They simply won't work.<br /> <br /> And that is, believe it or not, accurate... Outside of cities like Manaus, a big industrial city center in the middle of the amazonic rainforest here in Brazil, a cellphone won't work. Well, I live in Brazil, and I know that on the majority of the rural areas here, cellphones won't have a signal.<br /> <br /> No cover, or is it just that the technocratic Consensus is too weak in those places? Lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T16:12:10-08:00","id":1049547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049176#post1049176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd rather make WoD our world with additions and some substitutions. Endron instead of Shell, sure, but Snow fathered pathology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too. The more close it is to the real world (as much as possible, with all the WoD's bells and whistles), the better. Making it totally bonkers takes away the point of it, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T07:49:46-08:00","id":1049844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i> Endron instead of Shell, sure, but Snow fathered pathology.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>How it's that Shell being servants of an evil deity that spawns of monstrous mutant freaks by use of their corrupted products, that miraculously haven't been discovered by the masses in spite of having utterly dangerous and horrendous effects on normal people, is more believable that Dr. Snow case being an illuminaty style conspiracy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-16-2017, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T08:12:24-08:00","id":1049855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049450#post1049450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Phones don't exactly break down on the Amazon. They simply won't work.<br /> <br /> And that is, believe it or not, accurate... Outside of cities like Manaus, a big industrial city center in the middle of the amazonic rainforest here in Brazil, a cellphone won't work. Well, I live in Brazil, and I know that on the majority of the rural areas here, cellphones won't have a signal.<br /> <br /> No cover, or is it just that the technocratic Consensus is too weak in those places? Lol</div> </div> </div> </div>Coverage would only affect if they worked as phones, they should still work as computers if that was the only reason. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T08:20:40-08:00","id":1049862,"title":"","content":"Unless that's how Paradox manifests...<br /> <br /> But in all fairness I would argue that places where the phone doens't have signal are still reasonably within the Tech Rulz flag, that you can do all sort of stuff with the phone (you just can't use Data with it, but it's for a perfectly reasonable reason. Foci and stuff) while a place truly outside that flag should be much more eery, tech simply failing for no good reason","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T11:44:43-08:00","id":1049964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1049358#post1049358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, personally, like to believe that you can invent/discover new stuff in Mage without being Awakened. That Technocracy (or Mages, for what matters) don't rule the world to such a deep extent.<br /> <br /> I, however, don't explain this as &quot;Science it's 100% true&quot;, but rather as normal people working within the constraints of a Paradigm, expanding said Paradigm and thus slowly shaping the world. What normal people do it's also magic, it's just that it's paved within the limitations of what's already believed to be possible or plausible. Anyone that reads sci-fi knows that this it's a big leeway.<br /> <br /> Sorcerers can do stuff that isn't quite accepted by the Consensus by exploiting fringe aspects of the Consensus. They can go further than any normal person with a lot of willpower and dedication (note that I don't put supernaturals in this same bag).<br /> <br /> Mages think outside the box, they don't need to respect the Consensus. Ironically, I see Mages as closer that normal people to the true rules of Reality, the Universal Constants set there by the Pures and other primeval beings.<br /> Opening their minds to the full potential of humans, Mages understand more clearly what's truly subjective and what isn't (No one can radically change Gravity without a lot of effort, so it must be real, at least to some extent. Germs?, those may be relative, perhaps they're bad spirits that got into your body). They don't know everything instantly, and are limited to their preconceptions, but they can probe further than anyone else, and whatever they can't change, it's probably there to stay.<br /> <br /> This way I recognize the labor of the Technocracy pushing their Paradigm and manipulating the advancement of science according to the Time Table, but also recognize that a mundane scientist may gave them a surprise once in a blue moon.<br /> <br /> Also, I mantain that all Paradigms are equally valid AND invalid. Reality exists, but only as underlying principles that sometimes agree with science, and sometimes resist it's methods but are more agreeable to different approaches to knowledge<br /> <br /> Of course, this it's just an idea. Plenty of stuff in the bibliography to go for a &quot;harder&quot; or &quot;softer&quot; reality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This may be one of my favorite viewpoints I've read. I've never been a fan of the implication in mage that only Mages can make something new and that everyone else is mundane sheep that have to live in the world they are making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T12:28:54-08:00","id":1049993,"title":"","content":"There's quite a few ways to make sleepers investigation matter. 11twiggins method it's to make science the one true reality, then scientists can do meaningful research, and mages can't unless they adhere to science. Since I like the ideas of alternate viewpoints of reality, enlightement as the revelation of bigger truths, and mystics advancing magick by discoveryng new mystical truths, I take the opposite viewpoint, scientists can research, but they're advancing in one way of magic that isn't necessarily the only route for 'real' knowledge, mages are better at magic and thus can research better, but the sheer number of humans ensures that humanity can develop (slower) without enlightened aid .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T15:37:05-08:00","id":1050116,"title":"","content":"While I occasionally disagree with 11twiggins, I do agree that new scientific discoveries and new technological developments come from gaining understanding of objective reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T18:03:01-08:00","id":1050195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1048978-doctor-johnathan-snow-and-that-pesky-consensus?p=1050116#post1050116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I occasionally disagree with 11twiggins, I do agree that new scientific discoveries and new technological developments come from gaining understanding of objective reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the real world, sure, of course.<br /> <br /> But Mage is a fiction with djinns, flying carpets and demons... So, that's not exactly the same right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}